{:edb/db-before-t 928 :edb/db-after-t 929 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534241 50 #inst "2026-10-06T15:04:01.444Z" 13194139534241 true] [17592186064229 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282961 13194139534241 true] [17592186064229 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282989 13194139534241 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282968 13194139534241 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282975 13194139534241 true] [17592186064230 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282982 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282962 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1089 "q-104148" 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1100 "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ below have a discontinuity at $x=-\\sqrt{3}?$ \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{3}, & x<-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3, & x=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+3}, & x>-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1113 #uuid "d39d4010-b0be-5ef1-9cec-21d22a7b88ee" 13194139534241 true] [17592186282961 1145 "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- $f(-\\sqrt{3})=3,$ so $f(-\\sqrt{3})$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and find that they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{-}}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+3}{3} \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{+}}(\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)=2.\\,\\,✓$ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\n- The limit of the function is not equal to the function value: ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)=2,$ while $f(-\\sqrt{3})=3.$ $\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$ because ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)\\ne f(-\\sqrt{3}).$" 13194139534241 true] [17592186282962 1000 #edb/ref 17592